{"page":153,"blocks":[{"x":0.7305,"y":0.05257,"w":0.22101,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3.3 Differentiation Rules 139"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.09306,"w":0.48788,"h":0.01391,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Proof We apply the definition of the derivative to ƒ(x) = u(x) + y(x):"},{"x":0.55059,"y":0.10331,"w":0.28042,"h":0.04073,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3u(x + h) + y(x + h)4 - 3u(x) + y(x)4 h"},{"x":0.38311,"y":0.11354,"w":0.16221,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dx 3u(x) + y(x)4 = lim"},{"x":0.52221,"y":0.13372,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.52221,"y":0.15101,"w":0.14476,"h":0.03057,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0 c u(x + h) - u(x)"},{"x":0.74265,"y":0.15101,"w":0.06636,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"h d"},{"x":0.60818,"y":0.15144,"w":0.1938,"h":0.03007,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"h + y(x + h) - y(x)"},{"x":0.50522,"y":0.16077,"w":0.04011,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.54895,"y":0.18891,"w":0.10943,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"u(x + h) - u(x)"},{"x":0.70956,"y":0.18891,"w":0.11048,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y(x + h) - y(x)"},{"x":0.84504,"y":0.19104,"w":0.05722,"h":0.02794,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + dy"},{"x":0.76072,"y":0.1917,"w":0.10019,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"h = du"},{"x":0.50522,"y":0.19824,"w":0.04011,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.59958,"y":0.19824,"w":0.10636,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"h + lim"},{"x":0.88615,"y":0.19892,"w":0.02193,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.52221,"y":0.20866,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.68282,"y":0.20866,"w":0.02453,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"hS0"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.23676,"w":0.59307,"h":0.04351,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Combining the Sum Rule with the Constant Multiple Rule gives the Difference Rule, which says that the derivative of a difference of differentiable functions is the difference of their derivatives:"},{"x":0.54843,"y":0.28683,"w":0.14962,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx 3u + (-1)y4 = du"},{"x":0.68217,"y":0.28939,"w":0.09162,"h":0.02794,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + (-1) dy"},{"x":0.79881,"y":0.28939,"w":0.05722,"h":0.02794,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx - dy"},{"x":0.45233,"y":0.29006,"w":0.10789,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (u - y) = d"},{"x":0.75769,"y":0.29006,"w":0.05699,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx = du"},{"x":0.83992,"y":0.29727,"w":0.02193,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.32729,"w":0.58812,"h":0.03069,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The Sum Rule also extends to finite sums of more than two functions. If u1, u2, c, un are differentiable at x, then so is u1 + u2 + g + un, and"},{"x":0.71774,"y":0.36342,"w":0.10276,"h":0.02975,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + g+ dun"},{"x":0.48788,"y":0.3635,"w":0.20227,"h":0.02968,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (u1 + u2 + g+ un) = du1"},{"x":0.67167,"y":0.3635,"w":0.06456,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + du2"},{"x":0.80202,"y":0.37311,"w":0.02428,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx ."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.40381,"w":0.45637,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"For instance, to see that the rule holds for three functions we compute"},{"x":0.66945,"y":0.42392,"w":0.12968,"h":0.02977,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx (u1 + u2) + du3"},{"x":0.87278,"y":0.42392,"w":0.06456,"h":0.02975,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + du3"},{"x":0.78064,"y":0.424,"w":0.06456,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx = du1"},{"x":0.82671,"y":0.424,"w":0.06456,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + du2"},{"x":0.37104,"y":0.42639,"w":0.15556,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (u1 + u2 + u3) = d"},{"x":0.5148,"y":0.42639,"w":0.16645,"h":0.02729,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx ((u1 + u2) + u3) = d"},{"x":0.91886,"y":0.43361,"w":0.02428,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx ."},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.4643,"w":0.58674,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"A proof by mathematical induction for any finite number of terms is given in Appendix 2."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.49426,"w":0.44707,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 3 Find the derivative of the polynomial y = x3 + 4"},{"x":0.80147,"y":0.49614,"w":0.09989,"h":0.02507,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3x2 - 5x + 1."},{"x":0.53219,"y":0.53344,"w":0.03791,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx a4"},{"x":0.56193,"y":0.53344,"w":0.14057,"h":0.03052,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3x2b - d dx (5x) + d"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.53421,"w":0.12622,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"Solution dy dx = d"},{"x":0.47701,"y":0.53667,"w":0.06698,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dxx3 + d"},{"x":0.69068,"y":0.54388,"w":0.2103,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dx (1) Sum and Difference Rules"},{"x":0.52271,"y":0.57236,"w":0.21984,"h":0.0295,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"3 # 2x - 5 + 0 = 3x2 + 8 3x - 5"},{"x":0.45994,"y":0.57432,"w":0.07096,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 3x2 + 4"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.61745,"w":0.58894,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We can differentiate any polynomial term by term, the way we differentiated the poly- nomial in Example 3. All polynomials are differentiable at all values of x."},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.66006,"w":0.59305,"h":0.03329,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 4 Does the curve y = x4 - 2x2 + 2 have any horizontal tangents? If so, where?"},{"x":0.36259,"y":0.69698,"w":0.58172,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution The horizontal tangents, if any, occur where the slope dy>dx is zero. We have"},{"x":0.19645,"y":0.71868,"w":0.09561,"h":0.01461,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y = x4 −2x2 + 2"},{"x":0.53144,"y":0.72755,"w":0.05171,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = d"},{"x":0.57135,"y":0.73206,"w":0.2114,"h":0.02524,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx (x4 - 2x2 + 2) = 4x3 - 4x."},{"x":0.3626,"y":0.76758,"w":0.17468,"h":0.02246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Now solve the equation dy"},{"x":0.52185,"y":0.77657,"w":0.08699,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx = 0 for x:"},{"x":0.17216,"y":0.77974,"w":0.02835,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(0, 2)"},{"x":0.59592,"y":0.81046,"w":0.15253,"h":0.05632,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"4x3 - 4x = 0 4x(x2 - 1) = 0 x = 0, 1, -1."},{"x":0.10501,"y":0.82271,"w":0.12494,"h":0.0176,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(1, 1) (−1, 1) 1"},{"x":0.11002,"y":0.86513,"w":0.10912,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"0 1 −1"},{"x":0.36258,"y":0.87185,"w":0.59307,"h":0.06399,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"The curve y = x4 - 2x2 + 2 has horizontal tangents at x = 0, 1, and -1. The corre- sponding points on the curve are (0, 2), (1, 1), and (-1, 1). See Figure 3.11. We will see in Chapter 4 that finding the values of x where the derivative of a function is equal to zero is an important and useful procedure."},{"x":0.08775,"y":0.8914,"w":0.2482,"h":0.02762,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 3.11 The curve in Example 4 and its horizontal tangents."}]}